# Verdict schema (supporting file for the solotrace-audit skill)

Paste this as a quick-reference when writing verdicts.

```json
{
  "id": "REQ-01",
  "status": "covered",
  "reason": "Deposit limit enforced in services.py; boundary tests cover 0, negative, 50000.00, 50000.01.",
  "code_evidence": [
    { "file": "ledgerlite/services.py", "line": 123, "snippet": "if amount > _MAX_DEPOSIT:" }
  ],
  "test_evidence": [
    { "file": "ledgerlite/tests/test_spec2_deposit_limits.py", "test_name": "TestDepositValidation::test_boundary_50000_01_rejected" }
  ],
  "suggested_fix": null
}
```

**Rules:**
- `id` must match `^REQ-\d{2}$`
- `status` ∈ `{covered, untested, contradicts, missing}`
- `code_evidence[].line` must be an integer ≥ 1
- `suggested_fix` is optional (omit or set to null for covered verdicts)
